<!-- WHAT MASSAGE ACTUALLY DOES -->
<section class="au-beliefs" style="padding:100px 0;background:#f8f6f3">
  <div class="au-c">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:80px;align-items:start">
      <div class="au-in">
        <span class="au-tag" style="margin-bottom:16px;display:block">What We Believe</span>
        <h2 style="font-size:38px !important;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-bottom:28px !important;font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif !important;color:#111 !important;line-height:1.2 !important;font-weight:700 !important">What massage actually does — without the hype.</h2>
        <p style="color:#5c5c5c;font-size:17px !important;margin-bottom:18px !important;line-height:1.8 !important">We've seen too many stores overpromise. "This chair will change your life." "It cures back pain." The claims get bigger every year, and customers end up cynical — or worse, disappointed.</p>
        <p style="color:#5c5c5c;font-size:17px !important;margin-bottom:18px !important;line-height:1.8 !important">So we stick to what's real. Regular massage — done consistently — helps with stress, with tension, with sleep, with recovery. The Mayo Clinic talks about it. Sports medicine talks about it. Our customers talk about it. It's not a miracle. It's a routine that works when you actually use it.</p>
        <p style="color:#5c5c5c;font-size:17px !important;margin-bottom:0 !important;line-height:1.8 !important">The chair that gets used is the one that's in the right spot at the right time, that feels right the moment you sit down, that doesn't take any convincing. That's the chair we're trying to help you find.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="au-in" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px">
        <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e5e0d8;border-radius:14px;padding:32px 28px">
          <h3 style="font-size:17px !important;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif !important;font-weight:700 !important;color:#111 !important;margin-bottom:10px !important">Stress &amp; relaxation</h3>
          <p style="font-size:15px !important;color:#5c5c5c !important;line-height:1.7 !important">The most consistent thing we hear: people just feel calmer. Less reactive. Better at coping with the same workload. That's real — and it's enough reason for most people to keep using it.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e5e0d8;border-radius:14px;padding:32px 28px">
          <h3 style="font-size:17px !important;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif !important;font-weight:700 !important;color:#111 !important;margin-bottom:10px !important">Tension &amp; muscle recovery</h3>
          <p style="font-size:15px !important;color:#5c5c5c !important;line-height:1.7 !important">Desk pain, neck stiffness, lower back tension — these are the everyday complaints. Regular massage doesn't eliminate the source, but it gives the body somewhere to reset. Most people notice the difference within a few weeks.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e5e0d8;border-radius:14px;padding:32px 28px">
          <h3 style="font-size:17px !important;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif !important;font-weight:700 !important;color:#111 !important;margin-bottom:10px !important">Sleep &amp; mental load</h3>
          <p style="font-size:15px !important;color:#5c5c5c !important;line-height:1.7 !important">Ten minutes in the chair before bed. That's it. A lot of our customers end up using it less for pain and more just to signal to their body that the day is done. That's not nothing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Matt quote bar -->
    <div style="margin-top:56px;background:#111;border-radius:16px;padding:44px 48px;display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start">
      <svg style="width:32px;height:32px;fill:#b8944f;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:6px" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 17h3l2-4V7H5v6h3zm8 0h3l2-4V7h-6v6h3z"/></svg>
